WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.367
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.100
You're here.
Thank you for tuning in.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.868
Thank you for watching.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:09.767
Well, guys,
after a crazy four days,

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:13.267
March Madness is down
to the Sweet 16.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:15.267
That's right.
We are down to 16 teams.

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:16.767
Three number-one seeds

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:19.200
and nine million commercials
for AT&amp;T.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.701
Yeah.

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:22.968
Of course, the Cinderella story
that everyone's talking about

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:26.334
is the 15th-seed
Saint Peter's Peacocks

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.067
who have made it
to the Sweet 16.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.701
It's exciting for long-time fans

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:32.467
who have been following the team
since Thursday.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:34.334
[ Laughter ]
And, uh...

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:39.367
Saint Peter's is the first team
from New Jersey

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:42.234
to make the Sweet 16
in over 20 years.

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:43.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:47.133
Yeah, that's right.

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:49.000
And if they go all the way,
they'll be the only team

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.400
to wear their championship rings
on their pinkies.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:55.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:57.067
N-C-A-Ohh!

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:59.334
Hey! Ohh! This guy!

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:01.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:04.033
How can you not love their name?
They're the Peacocks.

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:06.000
This is the best thing
that happened to NBC

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.501
since the new "Law &amp; Order."

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:09.501
[ Laughter ]
I love it.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:10.701
Let's get to some news.

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.501
Well, guys, today
confirmation hearings began

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:16.100
for Supreme Court nominee
Ketanji Brown Jackson.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.868
The hearing process
will last four days.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:21.167
It's basically C-SPAN's version
of Coachella.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:22.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:24.767
And I saw that the top
Republican leading the hearings,

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:27.901
Chuck Grassley, is 88 years old.

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:29.634
Wow.
When it was his turn to speak,

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.133
he was like,
"Tell us who you are

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.767
and then tell me who I am."

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:35.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.000
Yep, Jackson will face days
of tough questions.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.434
Brett Kavanaugh was like...

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:41.133
[Slurring] "It'll be fine.
I did it for four days.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:45.200
After the s-second day...

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.968
After the --
After the second day,

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:48.400
it's kind of a blur. It's fine.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.601
It's like --

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:52.968
You're my best friend.
Hold my hair."

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:54.868
[ Imitates vomiting ]

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.467
But this is cool.

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:58.400
I saw that
Judge Jackson's parents

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.200
were at
the confirmation hearing.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.133
Even crazier,
so were Chuck Grassley's.

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:05.501
[ Laughter ]
-Really?!

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.534
-Hey, you guys
remember last year

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:11.367
when that huge ship
blocked up the Suez Canal?

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:15.167
Well, the same company that owns
that ship is back in the news,

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:17.300
and it's for exactly
the reason that you think.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.601
Listen to this.

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:21.133
-A massive cargo ship
is stuck in the mud

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:22.767
off the coast of Maryland.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:24.934
The vessel,
called the "Ever Forward,"

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:27.834
grounded in the Chesapeake Bay.

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:30.601
-Yeah, the "Ever Forward"
got stuck.

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:32.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:34.367
Which is why they're
renaming it the "Irony."

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:35.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:38.000
Every few months, the owner gets
a call from the captain like,

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.267
"Okay. Don't be mad..."

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:48.901
Well, listen to this.
I heard that Match just launched

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:52.400
a new dating app
for single parents called Stir.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.200
[ Audience ohhs ]
Yep.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.834
Their slogan is, "I'll join
your hell if you join mine."

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:58.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:01.133
[ Applause ]

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:07.067
And this is fun.
Today after a two-year hiatus,

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.968
Dairy Queen's
Free Cone Day returned!

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:11.133
-Wow!

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:13.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:14.968
-And after
their two-year hiatus,

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:17.934
the McDonald's ice-cream machine
is still on hiatus.

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:20.167
I'm sorry.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:23.767
Finally, guys, in Miami, a thief
broke into a sneaker store

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.400
and took 20 shoes.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.567
But when he got out, he realized
he only stole the left sneakers.

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:32.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:34.367
Officers were like --
[Imitates radio static]

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:35.868
"The suspect is 5'10",
200 pounds,

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:38.434
and running in circles."

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:39.834
No matter what happens,

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:42.734
I hope he realizes that 20 lefts
do not make a right.

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:44.267
We have a great show.

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:45.801
Give it up for the Roots,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:46.934
Thank you.

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:48.567
-[ Rapping ]

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:51.033
♪ Drop top... ♪

00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:53.367
♪ Attaboy...so savage ♪

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:56.267
♪ Making C's
seem so below average ♪

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:58.634
♪ Everyone in the cave... ♪

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:01.567
♪ Everybody know that...
like Bo Jackson ♪

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:04.501
♪♪

00:04:04.501 --> 00:04:08.267
-Hey, everyone! It is Monday!
We're excited to be back.

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:09.834
We have a great week
of shows ahead.

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:11.634
Ethan Hawke will be here
this week.

00:04:11.634 --> 00:04:12.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:15.234
Desus and Mero
will be joining us!

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:18.601
And Joe Jonas
will be here this week.

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:19.734
-Ohh!

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:23.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:24.167
And then
we'll also be talking --

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:26.100
I want to -- I want to --
Yeah, I know.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:28.133
I have a new book,
but we'll be talking about this.

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:30.033
-When?
-I don't want to do it now.

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:31.300
I don't know if I'm ready
to talk about it.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.667
-When are you gonna be ready
to talk about it?

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.067
-I don't know if I'm
ready to talk about it now.

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:36.734
-Really? When you don't want
to talk about "Nana Now"?

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:38.801
-It's not "Nana Now."
-Oh, it's "Nah-nah," right?

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:40.434
-No, it's not "Nah-Nah."
-Nah, nah, nah, nah.

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:42.267
-No, no. It's "Nana."
-"Nana."

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:44.968
-It's not "Nah-Nah."
It's "Nana Loves You More."

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:46.400
-Oh, okay.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.501
[ Audience awws ]

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:49.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.067
-This one's a weeper.
-Really?

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:53.467
-Yeah.
I finally wrote a cry one.

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:54.734
-You wrote a crying one?

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:56.400
-You know,
the books that come out,

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.901
and they're nice,
you get them for the babies

00:04:57.901 --> 00:04:59.133
and you get them
for the things --

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:00.467
And some are too sad.
-Yeah.

00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:01.968
-There's one that --
You know what I'm talking about.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.901
I'm not even gonna say the name.
-Oh, I know the one, I think.

00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:06.367
-It is awful. It is so sad.

00:05:06.367 --> 00:05:08.601
-Is it about carrying --
-Yeah, he's carrying his --

00:05:08.601 --> 00:05:10.167
"I'll Love You Forever."
That one?

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:12.834
-Don't say it.
I asked you not to say the name.

00:05:12.834 --> 00:05:15.501
It's too sad.
I had it removed from my house.

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:17.968
I said, "Appreciate the gift,
but please take it back."

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:20.234
-Yeah.
-Because it's too sad.

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:22.367
-She's carrying the baby,
then he carries the mom.

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:23.968
[ Audience awws ]

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:25.567
No, that's what I'm saying.
I can't do that.

00:05:25.567 --> 00:05:26.801
-My kids
wouldn't do that for me.

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:28.701
-No, I can't do it --
This is cute cry.

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:30.767
-Oh, cute cry. Good, good.
-This is like -- Yeah.

00:05:30.767 --> 00:05:32.534
Because who doesn't love
their grandma?

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:34.000
-Right.
-Their grammy.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.868
Their gam-gam. Their gigi.

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:40.601
Their abuela. Their memaw.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.968
What other names?
I got them all, right?

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:45.534
-You got them all.
-I got them all.

00:05:45.534 --> 00:05:47.100
It's cute. It's a good one.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:48.434
-But you don't want
to talk about it?

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:50.067
-No, I don't want
to talk about it.

00:05:50.067 --> 00:05:52.167
I don't want to talk about it.
No, not tonight.

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:53.267
I'll talk about it
maybe tomorrow.

00:05:53.267 --> 00:05:54.501
-Tomorrow?
-I want to have, like, a --

00:05:54.501 --> 00:05:57.167
I'm thinking of having
a theme week.

00:05:57.167 --> 00:05:59.334
But to do that, I --
It's a lot of scheduling.

00:05:59.334 --> 00:06:02.133
-You have to work.
Too much work.

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:03.868
-Guys, but what a show
we have for you tonight.

00:06:03.868 --> 00:06:06.534
She stars in the new movie
"The Bubble."

00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:08.300
Leslie Mann is here!

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.000
-Oh, I love her!
-Leslie Mann!

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:14.701
-I love Leslie Mann!
-I love Leslie Mann. Ohh.

00:06:14.701 --> 00:06:17.734
Speaking of love, you know him
from "Saturday Night Live."

00:06:17.734 --> 00:06:20.100
Now he's the host
of the number-one show

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.601
on Netflix right now,
"Is It Cake?"

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:24.067
Mikey Day is here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.067 --> 00:06:27.400
-Yeah!
-"Is It Cake?"

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.601
-Literally the best.
-"Is It Cake?"

00:06:29.601 --> 00:06:32.234
It's just a simple --
just simple rules.

00:06:32.234 --> 00:06:34.567
Is it or is it not cake?

00:06:34.567 --> 00:06:37.367
It's a fun game. I love it.

00:06:37.367 --> 00:06:39.801
And then we have --
Oh, my gosh. Fantastic music.

00:06:39.801 --> 00:06:41.734
Kae Tempest is here.
-Oh!

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:43.801 --> 00:06:45.501
-Kae Tempest is here!

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:48.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:48.767 --> 00:06:51.534
Very exciting.
Oh, this is big, actually.

00:06:51.534 --> 00:06:55.334
I saw that the daytime TV show
"Maury" is ending.

00:06:55.334 --> 00:06:56.934
-Oh.

00:06:56.934 --> 00:07:00.200
-Yeah. 31 years on the air
is quite a run.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:01.300
-Oh, man. That's a shame.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.067
"Maury" has been, like,
my favorite show.

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:04.434
-What?

00:07:04.434 --> 00:07:06.467
That's not true.

00:07:06.467 --> 00:07:07.868
"Maury" is not
your favorite show.

00:07:07.868 --> 00:07:10.267
I bet you've never even seen
an episode, you liar.

00:07:10.267 --> 00:07:13.067
-[ Scoffs ]
Don't you call me a liar!

00:07:13.067 --> 00:07:15.267
You don't even know me!
You're the liar!

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:16.267
[ Audience oohs ]

00:07:16.267 --> 00:07:18.567
-No, no, no, no, no. No.
You're the liar.

00:07:18.567 --> 00:07:20.634
-Whoa!
-You are!

00:07:20.634 --> 00:07:23.534
-Hey, hold on, guys, guys.
Calm down. Guys.

00:07:23.534 --> 00:07:26.000
-Know what? I don't need this.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.968
[Bleep] all y'all.
-Wait, wait, wait. What?!

00:07:27.968 --> 00:07:30.200
-Oh, yeah! You heard me!
-Boo!

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.234
-Boo!
-Boo him!

00:07:31.234 --> 00:07:33.467
-No, no, no, no, no, no! No!

00:07:33.467 --> 00:07:36.601
I don't need any of you!
Aah! Blegh!

00:07:36.601 --> 00:07:38.734
Forget it! [Fake sobbing]

00:07:38.734 --> 00:07:42.634
-You better run! Man, that's
all you ever do, is run!

00:07:42.634 --> 00:07:44.033
-Come on. Come on.

00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:45.934
[ Audience jeering ]

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:48.834
-[ Fake sobbing ]

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:56.200
-Higgins.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.334
You can't just storm out
every time you get upset.

00:07:58.334 --> 00:08:00.400
-You're right.
-You know? You have to learn

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:03.200
to confront your problem.
You know that?

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.767
-Yeah. I know that.
-You ready to go back out there?

00:08:06.767 --> 00:08:08.901
Let's do it.
Let's go back out there.

00:08:08.901 --> 00:08:10.133
-Yeah.
-Mm-hmm.

00:08:10.133 --> 00:08:12.300
Come on. Come on.
Let's go. Come on.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:15.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.801
-[ Fake sobbing ]

00:08:16.801 --> 00:08:19.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:24.567 --> 00:08:25.901
-That's alright.

00:08:25.901 --> 00:08:28.601
[ Laughter ]

00:08:31.601 --> 00:08:35.167
-[As Maury] Now we're gonna
get to the bottom of this.

00:08:35.167 --> 00:08:37.267
Higgins actually took
a lie-detector test

00:08:37.267 --> 00:08:41.734
before the show to prove
if he actually watches "Maury."

00:08:41.734 --> 00:08:44.100
Alright.
And here are the results.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:48.534
When asked, "Is 'Maury'
your favorite show?"

00:08:48.534 --> 00:08:51.067
Higgins said yes.

00:08:51.067 --> 00:08:52.734
-Yeah.

00:08:54.501 --> 00:08:59.801
-The lie detector determined
that was...

00:08:59.801 --> 00:09:01.200
a lie!
-Yeah!

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.667
-No! No!
-Yes! I told you!

00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:05.467
-No!
-Whoo-hoo! Whoo-hoo-hoo!

00:09:05.467 --> 00:09:09.300
-No! No! That's not --
Come on!

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:12.901
-Also, also,
our paternity test determined

00:09:12.901 --> 00:09:15.400
you're the father
of 28 illegitimate children.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.400
-I knew that.
-Oh, okay.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.801
Alright. Steve Higgins,
Tariq Trotter, everybody.

00:09:21.801 --> 00:09:24.801
Stick around. We're playing
charades with Leslie Mann

00:09:24.801 --> 00:09:27.100
and Mikey Day
when we come back, everybody.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:31.801
♪♪

